A CNAME makes one domain name point to another domain name.
A      fast-web-tech.co.uk     → 82.15.200.10
CNAME  www                     → fast-web-tech.co.uk

AAAA Record Points a domain to an IPv6 address.
AAAA  fast-web-tech.co.uk     → 2001:db8::1
A = IPv4
AAAA = IPv6
(AAAA = 4 × A = bigger address 😄)

MX Record Tells the internet which server handles email for your domain.

MX  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → mail.fast-web-tech.co.uk
“All emails like info@fast-web-tech.co.uk
 go to that mail server.”


TXT Record Stores text information for verification or security purposes.
TXT  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → google-site-verification=abc123
TXT  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all

NS Record Specifies the authoritative name servers for your domain.
NS  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → ns1.cloudflare.com
NS  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → ns2.cloudflare.com
NS  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → ns3.cloudflare.com
NS  fast-web-tech.co.uk  → ns4.cloudflare.com
